       new value at once and marks the element `[data-kp-updating]` with this
       register's `--kp-update` while the keyframes play. Two neon copies of
       the value, yellow right and up, cyan right and down, stand behind it
       and come home in four ticks (6, 4, 2, 1 px, then gone) over 480 ms;
       the value itself stays sharp on top and never moves. The copies are
       the value's own text-shadow, unblurred: the same glyphs, painted under
       the text, so a state word keeps its width-holding ::after and a cell
       its alignment, and no copy of the text is written anywhere. ── */
    [data-theme='cyberpunk'] {
