           writes the new value at once and marks its host
           `[data-kp-updating='plate']` for the update's time (the close's and
           the size's longer, times 1.25: 1200 ms; the fall is four fifths of
           it, 960): its red plate falls back into register on it. The value
           never moves. A state word keeps its width-holding ::after; a spark
           is an svg, whose parent carries the mark. */
        [data-theme='grotesk'] {
            --kp-update: plate;
        }

        [data-theme='grotesk'] [data-kp-updating='plate'] {
            --kp-sig-gr-r: 0.14em;
            animation: kp-sig-grotesk-update-plate calc(var(--kp-update-duration, 1200ms) * 0.8) linear backwards;
