       that traces everything"]: the pen traces the outline of what waits, then
       underlines every place a reading will stand, in reading order, the pen up
       between places. A place is two dimension ticks and a baseline the pen
       draws; places follow each other two units apart, so no two pens are ever
       on the sheet at once; a block of places is traced round first. A loop is
       18 units (2880 ms): the route, the marks standing, the marks lifted. The
       reduced pose is the marks standing, drawn, and no pen. The progress bar
       draws its value as a stroke with the pen at its end, busy it strokes along
